  "result": "All four tests pass.\n\n**What I did:** added `catalog/service.py` with the `NotFound` exception and the `Catalog` class from SPEC.md. Records live in a dict keyed by id, which preserves insertion order for `list()`. `get`, `update`, and `list` return copies so callers can't mutate internal state. `update` validates field names before touching the record, so an unknown field raises `ValueError` without partially applying changes.\n\n**Approach chosen:** Approach A, sequential integer ids from a per-catalog counter that only increases, so ids are never reused after a delete. This is a single-process, in-memory store with no need for cross-process coordination or unguessability, so the simpler, human-friendly, sortable ids are the better fit. Switching to UUIDs later would be a one-line change in the id-generation helper.",
